1325..1396 Comment "/// Spinning a sum is composing the spins (cubical\'s `intLoop-hom`), by"
1397..1470 Comment "/// induction on the second summand. `spin` puts its new loop first where"
1471..1548 Comment "/// cubical\'s `intLoop` puts it last, so the law composes the spins the other"
1549..1610 Comment "/// way round, as the words compute: `(loop ∷ p) then q` is"
1611..1689 Comment "/// `loop ∷ (p then q)` (#422). At zero `spin(Z)` is a call that returns the"
1690..1764 Comment "/// empty word, and the composite over it runs that call first (#473); the"
1765..1836 Comment "/// composites the arms carry convert through their definitions (#440)."
